{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "F24bOneIngestedColumnBreaksTheRecurrence",
  "description": "FINDING F24, SECOND REPRO — the SMALLEST document that shows it, and the one that names the trigger.\n\nIt is F24a's document with ONE ingested column added, and the recurrence DOES NOT READ THAT COLUMN. `m_monthID` comes from `runspecmonth` (one row, monthID 8) and is asserted separately so that the ingest is known to have worked; `s_clamped` is the same four-step recurrence, over the same `const` inputs, that F24a asserts and that passes there.\n\n    F24a (no data_sources)          esm test -> PASSES   [1, 3, 7, 15]\n    THIS FILE (one column ingested) esm test -> FAILS    [1, 1, 1, 1]\n\nSo the trigger is not \"the recurrence reads ingested data\". It is that THE DOCUMENT INGESTS AT ALL: `run_simulate` sets `build_pipeline = true` whenever providers exist, and on the build-pipeline path a causal self-read comes back unresolved. Add one column nothing reads and every recurrence in the document changes its answer.\n\nTHE FAILURE IS SILENT, AND THE CLAMP IS WHY. An unresolved self-read returns NaN, which would at least be loud. `max(NaN, 0)` returns 0 in this runtime, so a body with a clamp -- which is exactly what agedist.f has -- reads [1, 1, 1, 1] here: finite, plausible, monotone, wrong, and with nothing logged at any level. `s_value` is carried beside it as the unclamped control that reads NaN. CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.19.4 requires a raised fault rather than a sentinel and names this laundering as the reason.\n\nWHAT IT COSTS THIS PORT. fixtures/nr-logging-county.esm reads twenty-six snapshot tables, so it is on the pipeline path unconditionally -- and a fixture's emitted answer goes through `esm simulate`, which takes that path even for a document that does not ingest. Measured with agedist.f's fold wired in: `fold_totalPopulation` at 1991 read 1e-4 x (1 + grwfac) instead of 83.3 x (1 + grwfac), the signature of `max(self_read, MINGRWIND)` with an unresolved self-read, and the grown model-year fractions summed to 1.5e-06 instead of 4.697819. components/age_distribution.esm computes the same fold correctly and asserts it in 55 places, because it does not ingest.",
  "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
  "tags": ["finding", "recurrence", "aggregate", "silent", "expected-to-fail", "data-sources"]
 },
 "data_sources": {
  "f24_runspecmonth": {
   "kind": "static",
   "source": {
    "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/nr-logging-county/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
   },
   "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_f24_runspecmonth" },
   "metadata": { "tags": ["runspec"], "esio_format": "parquet",
     "note": "One row, monthID 8. The smallest table in the snapshot, chosen because the point is that ANY ingest is enough -- the recurrence never reads it." }
  }
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "n_f24_runspecmonth": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Rows in runspecmonth, discovered by the source's own extent. 1." }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "step_rows": { "kind": "interval", "size": 4 },
  "month_rows": { "kind": "interval", "size": "n_f24_runspecmonth" }
 },
 "models": {
  "F24bOneIngestedColumnBreaksTheRecurrence": {
   "tolerance": { "rel": 0.0, "abs": 0.0 },
   "variables": {
    "m_monthID": {
     "type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0, "shape": ["month_rows"],
     "description": "runspecmonth.monthID. Read only so that the document INGESTS, and asserted only so that a failure cannot be blamed on the ingest not having happened.",
     "update": { "kind": "data", "source": "f24_runspecmonth", "from": { "file_variable": "monthID" } }
    },
    "m_month": {
     "type": "unknown", "units": "1",
     "description": "The ingested month as a scalar, 8. Nothing else reads it."
    },
    "s_value": {
     "type": "unknown", "shape": ["step_rows"], "units": "1",
     "description": "s[1] = 1, s[k] = 2 x s[k-1]: [1, 2, 4, 8]. The unclamped control. Reads [1, NaN, NaN, NaN] here."
    },
    "s_clamped": {
     "type": "unknown", "shape": ["step_rows"], "units": "1",
     "description": "s[1] = 1, s[k] = 2 x max(s[k-1], 0) + 1: [1, 3, 7, 15]. The shape agedist.f has. Reads [1, 1, 1, 1] here, because max(NaN, 0) is 0."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "m_month",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate", "args": [], "output_idx": [],
      "ranges": { "j": { "from": "month_rows" } },
      "expr": { "op": "index", "args": ["m_monthID", "j"] }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "s_value",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate", "args": [], "output_idx": ["k"],
      "ranges": { "k": { "from": "step_rows" } },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        { "op": "<=", "args": ["k", 1] },
        1.0,
        { "op": "*", "args": [
          { "op": "index", "args": ["s_value", { "op": "-", "args": ["k", 1] }] },
          2.0] }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "s_clamped",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "aggregate", "args": [], "output_idx": ["k"],
      "ranges": { "k": { "from": "step_rows" } },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        { "op": "<=", "args": ["k", 1] },
        1.0,
        { "op": "+", "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "max", "args": [
              { "op": "index", "args": ["s_clamped", { "op": "-", "args": ["k", 1] }] },
              0.0] },
            2.0] },
          1.0] }
       ]
      }
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "one_ingested_column_does_not_change_a_recurrence",
     "description": "INTENDED behaviour, at ZERO tolerance: the ingest delivers monthID 8, and the two recurrences give what they give in F24a, which is [1, 2, 4, 8] and [1, 3, 7, 15]. OBSERVED: the month arrives correctly, `s_value` reads NaN from step 2 on, and `s_clamped` reads 1 at every step. The month assertion passing while the recurrences fail is what makes the finding attributable: the data path works, and it is the RECURRENCE that the pipeline build changes.",
     "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
     "assertions": [
      { "variable": "m_month", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.0 },
      { "variable": "s_value", "time": 0.0, "expected": 2.0, "coords": { "step_rows": 2 } },
      { "variable": "s_value", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.0, "coords": { "step_rows": 4 } },
      { "variable": "s_clamped", "time": 0.0, "expected": 3.0, "coords": { "step_rows": 2 } },
      { "variable": "s_clamped", "time": 0.0, "expected": 15.0, "coords": { "step_rows": 4 } }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
